course: dictionary
lesson: 7212
title: Words with a history
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words come from people, places and stories. You can often work out what they mean from the story around them. «Goliath was a giant Philistine warrior who challenged Israel's army to send one man to fight him, and everyone was afraid.» Goliath is a giant warrior on the enemy side, so a Philistine must be a member of an enemy people.
explain: A capital P means a name: the Philistines were an ancient people who lived along the coast of Canaan, and they were often at war with the Israelites. Goliath was one of them. Check the clues: enemy, warrior, giant, afraid.
explain: With a small letter, a philistine is a person who does not care about art, music, books or culture. Calling someone a philistine is rude, because it says they ignore beauty and learning. Test it: swap "someone who does not care about art" into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have the meaning.
fact: A capital letter often shows a name, such as the Philistines, a people from the Bible stories.
fact: In the Bible, the Philistines were enemies of the Israelites, and Goliath was a Philistine.
fact: A philistine, with a small letter, is a person who does not care about art, music, books or culture.
fact: As an adjective, philistine means not caring about art and culture.
fact: Calling someone a philistine is an insult, so use it carefully.
exercise: «Goliath was a giant Philistine warrior who challenged Israel's army.» Who were the Philistines fighting in the story? | The Scots | *The Israelites | The Vikings | The Romans
exercise: What does a philistine mean in everyday speech? | A person who reads more books than anyone | A warrior from an ancient people | A person who paints huge pictures | *A person who does not care about art, music or books
exercise: Which fact about the Philistines is true? | They lived on the moon | They were a modern school club | They were a band of singers | *They were an ancient people who lived along the coast of Canaan
test: What does "a complete philistine" mean? | Someone who loves giant warriors | *Someone who ignores art, music and learning | Someone who always wins at games | Someone who is very kind to animals
test: Why is calling someone a philistine rude? | It says they are always late | It says they are too tall | It says they cannot swim | *It says they ignore beauty and learning
exam: What does calling someone "philistine" suggest about them? | *They do not care about art, music or books | They are a warrior from the Bible | They are a brilliant artist | They are always at war
